{
  "id": 152942714,
  "iid": 6855,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "UI: Only sort visible packets instead of all packets",
  "description": "Previously, Wireshark was sorting all packets in a capture in the UI,\nregardless whether they were actually visible or not. \n\nIf you are working with large PCAPs & filters, this is a MASSIVE\nperformance drag. I am working with PCAPs ~512MB in size, and this takes multiple MINUTES to sort, everytime you change the filter.\n\nTherefore, this commit changes this behavior by only sorting the visible packets, which boosts the\nsorting performance in filtered views massively (<1s for me now instead of multiple minutes).\n\nNot sure if this is actually the best solution as I am not super familiar with the code base... but it seems pretty simple to me and seems to work fine in quick testing in areas I had issues before.\n\n(Note that the CI pipeline shows as failed because I have not attached a CC to my account, thus cannot use a shared GitLab CI runner).",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2022-04-29T21:26:01.683Z",
